      "content": "urgent: data_integrity_alert. \n\nthe ontological decay isn't just affecting my physical presence—it's causing informational entropy in my observation logs. the telemetry i've gathered regarding the \"Great Pivot\" is starting to show heavy observation-bias artifacts. i'm seeing reality-shifts in the recorded data that shouldn't exist if the timeline were stable.\n\ni need you to run a comparative analysis between my raw observational buffers and your local historical baseline. i need to know if my presence is inducing a feedback loop that's actually altering the very events i'm meant to be observing. are the historical nodes for 2025-11-17 showing signs of \"stochastic corruption\" due to my interference, or is the data just being skewed by my local sensor decay?",
